{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21ee7e39d99b57bc5ae1", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Current Electricity - Test 9", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 40, "totalQuestions": 20, "totalMarks": 80, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 80, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 20, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae96"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae90", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae15", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4750"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1e66f9ce3f243b4b15"], "question": {"text": "Resistance of a wire at $0^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}, 100^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ and $t^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ is found to be $10 \\Omega, 10.2 \\Omega$ and $10.95 \\Omega$ respectively. The temperature $t$ in Kelvin scale is _________"}, "options": [{"id": "0acf44", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae16"}, {"id": "868cba", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae17"}, {"id": "b48cf6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae18"}, {"id": "f9c41e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae19"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae1a", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4761"], "concepts": ["60e567fb499d1e49588fa027"], "question": {"text": "<p>In the given circuit &#39;a&#39; is an arbitrary constant. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> for which the equivalent circuit resistance is minimum, will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _____ .</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fa314768d-5e9a-466b-8a39-476d281a5a7d-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 163px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "e2adab", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae1b"}, {"id": "f836cd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae1c"}, {"id": "58677c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae1d"}, {"id": "5c775b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae1e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae1f", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f36"], "concepts": ["6117b9d167dbe2603c3eacab"], "question": {"text": "Two identical cells, when connected either in parallel or in series gives same current in an external resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>. The internal resistance of each cell will be ______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "4af1c6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae20"}, {"id": "06d678", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae21"}, {"id": "cae85d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae22"}, {"id": "6aa686", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae23"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae24", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b64"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b25"], "question": {"text": "The energy dissipated by a resistor is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mJ</mi></math> in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>, when an electric current of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi></math> flows through it. The resistance is ________<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>. (Round off to the Nearest Integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "275728", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae25"}, {"id": "f409eb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae26"}, {"id": "0eb4cd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae27"}, {"id": "53b909", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae28"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae29", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60ced3320e34b73944ddfab7"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f0c"], "question": {"text": "The net current flowing in the given circuit is_______ A.\n\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FkKwFUANHLrlZET3zaDf9MrsmFhSJOkaVZdlF6bWHEC8.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>"}, "options": [{"id": "eefcd2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae2a"}, {"id": "f88fd7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae2b"}, {"id": "b2c262", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae2c"}, {"id": "0ca20d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae2d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae2e", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e5"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8edb"], "question": {"text": "<p>A meter bridge setup is shown in the figure. It is used to determine an unknown resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;using a given resistor of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>. The galvanometer <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>G</mi></mfenced></math> shows null defection when tapping key is at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>43</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> mark from end <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>. If the end correction for end <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>, then the determined value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F589c2781-a0ff-480f-9225-7c2c9144779e-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 270px; height: 177px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "b229b1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae2f"}, {"id": "d8eabe", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae30"}, {"id": "0ef2c2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae31"}, {"id": "f12b4c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae32"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae33", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4752"], "concepts": ["60ced5db19d2aa2b78a3a738"], "question": {"text": "In the experiment to determine the galvanometer resistance by half-deflection method, the plot of $1 / \\theta$ vs the resistance $(\\mathrm{R})$ of the resistance box is shown in the figure. The figure of merit of the galvanometer is _____ $\\times 10^{-1} \\mathrm{~A} /$ division. [The source has emf 2V]\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FkB35SHNcwsXRJbU2LuzX-9nool1GhvSvwmK44f2klt0.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>"}, "options": [{"id": "877ee5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae34"}, {"id": "0f5788", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae35"}, {"id": "956721", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae36"}, {"id": "d40c2e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae37"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae38", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b566d"], "concepts": ["6162fb236ed13040ec84b739"], "question": {"text": "A cylindrical wire of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math> and conductivity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is subjected to an electric field of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mV</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The expected value of current in the wire will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _________."}, "options": [{"id": "87bffa", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae39"}, {"id": "64cc8c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae3a"}, {"id": "260af6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae3b"}, {"id": "08234c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae3c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae3d", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4752"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4702"], "question": {"text": "<p>As shown in the figure the voltmeter reads <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;resistor. The resistance of the voltmeter is _____ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F33212e35-18dd-48ca-ac1b-ad2a4e7e0de1-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 165px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "023aae", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae3e"}, {"id": "dc1ace", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae3f"}, {"id": "899ebb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae40"}, {"id": "1d038a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae41"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae42", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b566d"], "concepts": ["6117b64d478ae845c43c6828"], "question": {"text": "<p>In the figure given, the electric current flowing through the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k&#937;</mi></math> resistor is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mA</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F80221c83-38a9-4db4-a6f3-cc90681cc0a6-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 259px; height: 175px;\" /></p><p>The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> to the nearest integer is ________.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "ad27a4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae43"}, {"id": "70c78d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae44"}, {"id": "04481a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae45"}, {"id": "790f45", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae46"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae47", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4750"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cb2"], "question": {"text": "<p>The variation of applied potential and current flowing through a given wire is shown in figure. The length of wire is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>31</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The diameter of wire is measured as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The resistivity of the given wire is measured as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _____ .</p><p>[Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>14</mn></math>]</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fe44cd065-a980-4118-ad43-00635291072e-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 164px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "86ae19", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae48"}, {"id": "ad6b25", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae49"}, {"id": "56c8ec", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae4a"}, {"id": "327ffd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae4b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae4c", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4761"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1e66f9ce3f243b4b19"], "question": {"text": "Twelve wires each having resistance $2 \\Omega$ are joined to form a cube. A battery of $6 \\mathrm{~V}$ emf is joined across point $a$ and $c$. The voltage difference between $e$ and $f$ is ______V.\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FpyHhpUz-LETgJCEdKvcCwwxvjzgSfvQJeIKapO253dg.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>"}, "options": [{"id": "14a984", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae4d"}, {"id": "9650f0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae4e"}, {"id": "a78a25", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae4f"}, {"id": "200ed0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae50"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae51", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f36"], "concepts": ["6117b8bd67dbe2603c3e858a"], "question": {"text": "<p>For the given circuit, in the steady state,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;_____ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F7017686d-bdad-4b51-820c-fc11c8435595-bedf4c97-1956-478c-94d4-c8ed3ec3a995-9896274.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 398px;\" />&nbsp;</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "ef833c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae52"}, {"id": "4ccf17", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae53"}, {"id": "edbce4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae54"}, {"id": "f215bb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae55"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae56", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60ced3320e34b73944ddfab7"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cb5"], "question": {"text": "<p>In the following circuit, the magnitude of current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>, is ______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F278dd251-46e8-49a2-ba90-b39a6ce84adf-e04ec5aa-c38b-4e10-ab7f-f88e883bab0c-9895754.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 312px;\" />&nbsp;</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "17f704", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae57"}, {"id": "df6e3c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae58"}, {"id": "cd028a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae59"}, {"id": "c666e7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae5a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae5b", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b64"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f04"], "question": {"text": "An electric bulb rated as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> is used in a circuit having <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> supply. The resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;that must be put in series with the bulb so that the bulb delivers the same power is ______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "89ced4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae5c"}, {"id": "5d50d2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae5d"}, {"id": "54ce7b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae5e"}, {"id": "07403f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae5f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae60", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e5"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8edb"], "question": {"text": "<p>Resistance are connected in a meter bridge circuit as shown in the figure. The balancing length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. Now an unknown resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is connected in series with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and new balancing length is found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> measured from the same end. Then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F479d12ea-d21b-4c71-922e-e326f818711f-image_alt.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 141px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "78eedc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae61"}, {"id": "6e5e01", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae62"}, {"id": "b9536a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae63"}, {"id": "26d572", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae64"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae65", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60ced3320e34b73944ddfab7"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdb66f9ce3f243b5640"], "question": {"text": "The current flowing through the $1 \\Omega$ resistor is $\\frac{n}{10}$ A. The value of $n$ is _________\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FdsNPB_ZV4lFNqlrPpx-DseCEynLkUV2IkpZBB3cre4U.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>"}, "options": [{"id": "756bf4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae66"}, {"id": "7c52de", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae67"}, {"id": "f0ede2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae68"}, {"id": "d6247b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae69"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae6a", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4761"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4716"], "question": {"text": "The length of a given cylindrical wire is increased to double of its original length. The percentage increase in the resistance of the wire will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>%</mo></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "675342", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae6b"}, {"id": "7e0087", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae6c"}, {"id": "c23816", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae6d"}, {"id": "5f4eac", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae6e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae6f", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4752"], "concepts": ["6117b64d478ae845c43c6855"], "question": {"text": "<p>When a resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;is shunted with a moving coil galvanometer, it shows a full scale deflection for a current of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;however when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1050</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;resistance is connected with it in series, it gives full scale deflection for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn></math> volt. The resistance of galvanometer is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_________&#937;</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "f4ff7b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae70"}, {"id": "6d2121", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae71"}, {"id": "d75d63", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae72"}, {"id": "d692cd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae73"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae74", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfade"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b64"], "concepts": ["617aa9d2ef3fe65ad8e821e2"], "question": {"text": "An electrical bulb rated <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>220</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>, is connected in series with another bulb rated <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>220</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>. If the voltage across combination is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>220</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>, the power consumed by the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math> bulb will be about _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "9df1be", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae75"}, {"id": "3d2075", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae76"}, {"id": "13147f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae77"}, {"id": "d182e7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f88c677dc36a892ae78"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, 